    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0230" n="199" xml:id="pg199"/>

                <head>60. Note From the Executive Secretary of the Department of State (Levitsky) to the Deputy Secretary of State
                        (Whitehead)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d60-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1988-06-29">June 29, 1988</date></dateline>
                    <salute>John:</salute></opener>
                <!--<pb facs="d60-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="d60-2"/>-->
                <p>The NSC staff memo<anchor n="2" xml:id="d60-f2"
                    /> was given to the Secretary by Colin. Apparently Rodman and Ledsky are trying
                    to make a big thing of this. I think they’re wrong as you will see from my
                    comments on their paper.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >Mel</hi></signed></closer>
                <!--<pb facs="d60-3" n="3" type="facsimile" xml:id="d60-3"/>-->


                <xi:include href="d60-a1.xml" xpointer="d60-a1"/>
